    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0468" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg372"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New London,
                                Conn.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-07-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon receipt of your note No. 1054, of the
                    15th ultimo, I fully notified Her Majesty’s principal secretary of state for
                    foreign affairs <pb facs="0469" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/> that the Congress of
                    the United States had made the necessary appropriation to enable the United
                    States Government to discharge its obligations under the treaty of February 8,
                    1898, and the award of the commission organized in accordance therewith.</p>
                <p>I have now received a dispatch from the Marquis of Salisbury, desiring me to
                    express to you the satisfaction felt by the Government of Her Majesty at the
                    final settlement of these claims.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
